      "line_no": 1,
      "code": "UPDATE Customers",
      "explanation": "This example shows that not only one, more than one condition can be defined in one SQL."
    },
    {
      "line_no": 2,
      "code": "     SET cust_rep = 102",
      "explanation": ""
    },
    {
      "line_no": 3,
      "code": "     WHERE cust_rep IN (105, 106, 107);",
      "explanation": "IN is the set membership test. It tests whether a data value matches one of a list of target values. In this example, if cust_rep is one of 105,106, or 107, the condition turns out TRUE."
